# tests/leak-patterns — your PRIVATE identifier list. Copy to tests/leak-patterns
# (gitignored) and fill in yours. One ERE per line; '#' comments and blank lines
# are skipped. Patterns are validated before use; an invalid line fails the scan.
#
# List things that must NEVER appear in this repo: AWS account IDs, employer and
# product names, internal hostnames, project codewords, old email addresses.
# Do NOT list your public attribution (your name, GitHub handle, the repo URL):
# it belongs in LICENSE/README/SETUP by design. Put those in tests/attribution
# (also gitignored) — the publication gate allows them only under LICENSE,
# README.md, SETUP.md, and docs/.
123456789012                    # an AWS account id (example)
234567890123                    # another account you use (example)
old-employer-name|oldproduct
internal-hostname
first\.last@old-employer\.com
